+# AWS Inferentia / Trainium Runbook (end-to-end)
+
+Prereqs:
+- AWS account and access to Neuron-enabled AMIs or instance families (inf1 for Inferentia, trn1 for Trainium).
+- Neuron SDK access and license (vendor-provided).
+
+Steps:
+1. Create a Neuron nodegroup:
+   eksctl create nodegroup --cluster my-cluster --name inferentia --node-type inf1.6xlarge --nodes 1 --nodes-min 1 --nodes-max 3 --labels inferentia=true
+
+2. Install Neuron drivers and runtime on AMI or via bootstrap script. Use AWS-provided AMIs where possible.
+
+3. Deploy device plugin (ops/hw/device_plugins/aws-neuron-daemonset.full.yaml).
+
+4. Build the neuron image in secure builder (ops/hw/inferentia/Dockerfile.neuron). Push to internal registry.
+
+5. Deploy inference server pointing to INFERENCE_BACKEND=INFERENTIA and the neuron image. Use helm values to set nodeSelector tolerations.
+
+6. Run validation:
+   - Use ops/ci/load_test_async.py to exercise endpoint.
+   - Monitor node logs and /opt/neuron presence.
+
+Notes:
+- Building neuron images must happen in a secure environment with access to neuron packages.
+- Replace placeholder neuron inference calls with your compiled neuron models (torch-neuronx compiled artifacts).
